Package: SPHARM.analysis
Title: Characterizing Core Scar Patterning and Morphology within a Unified
    Spherical Harmonic Framework
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Peiyuan", "Xiao", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0000-9733-5875")),
    person("Hao", "Li", role = "aut", email = "lihao@itpcas.ac.cn",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0008-1504-9401")),
    person("Ben", "Marwick", role = "aut", email = "bmarwick@uw.edu",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-7879-4531")))
Description: Research compendium with the data and code to reproduce the
    analyses and figures in the paper "Characterizing core scar patterning
    and morphology within a unified spherical harmonic framework". The
    workflow couples R preprocessing, Python spherical-harmonic (SPHARM)
    analysis of core meshes and scar-orientation kernel-density estimates,
    and R statistical analysis, orchestrated as a single reproducible
    'targets' pipeline.
Imports:
    quarto,
    visNetwork
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
SystemRequirements: Docker; Python (conda environment 'spharm',
    see analysis/scripts/environment.yml); Quarto
URL: https://github.com/PeiyuanXiao/SPHARM_analysis
